WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:27.750
A Whale That Sang a Song

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.000
Good morning!

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:31.420
Good morning.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:31.960
Morning.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.040
Oh, good! I got in before Asuma.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:38.550
The midnight movie was "Gondam,"
which I hadn't seen in years!

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.470
I first saw it when I
was in elementary sch...

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:45.890
You slacker! A policeman's hours are
not just 9 to 5! We're on duty 24/7!

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:47.520
Yeah, yeah, I forgot.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:49.440
Oh? You got a letter?

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.270
Uh-huh, it's from home.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.820
Hey, it's a whale! Hiromi, do they
have whales where you grew up?

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:00.740
You don't see too many these days,
but I used to see a lot when I was a kid.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.660
In winter they approach
the shore to breed.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.500
Wow! Is that you, Hiromi?

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:13.250
Back in elementary school. See that
dark line behind me? That's a whale.

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:14.750
A humpback whale, isn't it?

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:15.630
That's right.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.800
They're an endangered species
that almost became extinct.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:22.050
Is that true?
I'd love to see one just once.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.510
It's a sight you'll never forget, Noa.

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:25.720
Morning, guys!

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.060
Well, well! Looks like I'm the last one.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:31.230
What's the meaning of this, Shinohara?
You have no respect for the badge!

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.940
Don't you know that a...

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.690
"A policeman's hours are not just 9 to 5."

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:36.900
Anyway, you gotta check this out.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.320
Whoa! Is that Okinawa?

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:43.860
Don't be silly. It's Tokyo Bay.

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:45.030
Tokyo Bay?

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.080
Better believe it! It's
swimming inside the levee.

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:52.000
The whale was first spotted in
Tokyo Bay early this morning.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:54.330
Experts have since identified it
as a humpback whale...

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:58.250
but no one knows why or how
the whale wound up here in the bay.

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:03.680
That's very odd. I don't think I've ever
heard of whales coming so close to shore.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.970
They're known to be very
cautious creatures by nature.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:09.770
You think maybe the little guy got lost?

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.600
"The little guy"? You mean the whale?

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:12.180
Uh-huh.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:13.020
Oh, boy...

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:15.650
There's gotta be a way we can help him?

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:18.900
Animal rights groups are
already on the case, I'm sure.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.440
And the government has
an obligation, too.

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:26.070
Waste of time! The government has better
things to do than help little lost whales!

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:31.790
Ota, do you realize how many species
are in danger of extinction?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.210
The whales, especially...

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.750
OK! Um... how about some tea, huh?

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:40.750
There haven't been any big cases lately.
Ota feels awfully frustrated, you know?

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:41.510
Hmm.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.010
It's still a waste of time!

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:44.470
Shut up!

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:50.680
As you can see, here at Takeshiba Pier,
crowds are flocking to catch a glimpse...

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.140
of the rare and unexpected visitor.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:55.230
But what is to become of the whale?

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.480
Clearly, a whale cannot survive in the
filthy maze we call... Tokyo Bay.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:02.530
Hello. This is Eyewitness TV.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:03.860
I'm calling about
that whale in Tokyo Bay.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:07.320
Can't somebody do something?
I feel awful for that thing.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:08.660
But, sir...

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:11.990
We've got to save him!
What's the government doing?

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:14.500
Oh, yes, the whale in Tokyo Bay!

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:18.500
My goodness, that poor thing!
You know, whales are very intelligent.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:22.130
We must protect the wildlife.
It's our duty to act.

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:25.970
It's terrible!
Somebody do something, please!

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:30.550
Sign the petition to save the whale!
Together we can save the whale!

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.180
We need your help!

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:35.310
...and the visiting American ambassador
urged the Prime Minister to...

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:38.150
take aggressive measures to save
the whale in Tokyo Bay.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:40.770
Save the whale!

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:43.610
Save the whale!

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:46.070
Thank you all for writing!
And since he's a humpback...

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:50.490
we've decided to name our guest
in Tokyo Bay "Humpy"!

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:53.040
Whale Problem in Tokyo Bay

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:55.000
Saving the Whale

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.540
Over 100,000 Signatures Collected

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.630
Tokyo Bay
Whale Rescue Committee

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.930
In addition to the environmental
hazards of Tokyo Bay...

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:10.470
this whale situation has attracted
worldwide attention.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:15.060
This matter demands the maximum
cooperation from all ministries involved.

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:19.600
The Maritime Safety Agency will act
as the hub of operation...

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.690
and implement the rescue mission.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.360
Also, the Fire Department
will be our backup...

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:27.860
Hiromi, you must be happy
to be part of the rescue.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:28.490
Yeah.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:29.610
We can do it!

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:32.490
All ministries stay on full
alert pending the entire operation!

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:36.120
Now, let us move on to the specifics
of the rescue plan...

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:37.040
Excuse me.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:37.830
Huh?

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.750
What are WE supposed to do, Ms. Takao?

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.500
Division 2 will handle...

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:56.770
If you're not in line for the ferry,
please move your vehicles immediately.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:07:01.900
Do not obstruct traffic! Vehicles in the
prohibited zone will be removed by Labors.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:08.070
I repeat: Vehicles in the prohibited zone
will be removed by Labors.

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:14.490
Damn! There are too many idiots
with too much free time on their hands!

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.870
Reporting live from above Tokyo Bay!

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:24.250
We're flying over the site where the
Rescue Committee is about to begin...

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:25.420
their heroic undertaking
to rescue Humpy!

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:31.930
Wow! That's neat!
I'll take three, please!

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:32.720
Coming up!

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:33.340
Uh!

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:36.560
What are you doing?
You aren't here on vacation, you know.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:40.060
But, Asuma! There's so much
downtime until our shift.

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:41.810
Here you go, three whales!

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:49.490
Civilian vessels are prohibited inside
Tokyo Bay today.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:52.950
For your own safety,
return to port immediately.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:56.240
I repeat: Civilian vessels are prohibited
inside Tokyo Bay today.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:59.200
For your own safety,
return to port immediately.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:00.540
That's so cool!

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:01.710
Don't say that.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:02.460
Why not?

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.630
It only points out how uncool our job is.

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:09.880
This car is parked illegally!
It will be removed.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:13.300
Move away from my feet!
It's dangerous here!

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:17.180
Traffic regulation IS a crucial
element of the rescue.

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.940
The Maritime Safety Agency
has deployed an impressive fleet.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:31.150
Will the poor suffering whale be
safely brought back to the open sea?

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.990
What specific steps will be taken to
ensure the rescue?

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:37.410
And now, the question of the day:
Can you guess the exact date and time...

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:40.200
Humpy will finally make it
out of the bay?

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:43.160
Send your predictions
to this address here!

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:46.120
Begin the operation!
Formation A!

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.220
Target spotted:
500 meters, forward.

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:03.180
Good. Formation B!

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:08.230
They're moving in.

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:12.360
Looks like the Rescue Committee's
historic operation is now under way.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:25.710
That's it. Keep going. Go on, swim
out of the bay, to the sea.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:30.420
- There it goes.
- Wow, look at that!

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:38.680
Nobody wants to look at
my Patlabor today.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:44.310
- Wow, look at that.
- Is he heading out?

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:46.020
I can't see.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:49.940
Hey, you can't stand there!
You're blocking our view!

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:55.440
OK, OK! Ota,
I can relieve you now. Ota?

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:57.530
Hey, out of the way!

00:09:57.570 --> 00:10:00.240
- C'mon! I can't see!
- Get that Labor outta here!

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:03.450
They're taxpayers! They're taxpayers!
They pay for the Labors!

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:05.330
You tax thieves!

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:06.870
What did you say?

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:09.040
Capitalist scum!
Rapists of the environment!

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:11.420
Don't tell me you elitist pigs care
about the whales all of a sudden!

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:14.500
You unconscionable hypocrites!

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:16.510
You're a menace to Nature!

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:20.890
You should be ashamed of yourselves!
Wake up and smash Babylon Project now!

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:23.930
Y-You Communist agitators!

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:28.520
Oh, no!

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:30.190
Ota, calm down!

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:32.690
Ota, no!

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:36.150
Yamazaki, get out of the way!
I don't want to hurt you!

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.320
Ha! You don't have the GUTS!

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.030
Oh, yeah? Watch THIS!

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:41.030
Don't do it!

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:44.870
Whoa!

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:47.290
Ooops.

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:52.130
Damn you!
You'll be hearing from our lawyers!

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:59.470
Homework.
Bring it back tomorrow morning.

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:00.930
Yes, sir!

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:06.970
Hey, Yamazaki.

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:08.480
Yes, sir?

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:11.560
Don't let those two suck
you in again, huh?

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:15.110
I'm sorry, Captain. Excuse me.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:19.740
News Terminal

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:23.870
Good evening, this is News Terminal.

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:26.620
First, the story that's captivated
the whole world:

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.870
The Tokyo Bay
Whale Rescue Mission has failed...

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:32.170
despite the government's
concerted efforts today.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:35.250
A fleet of ships surrounded and pursued
the whale toward the ocean...

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:39.340
but the whale managed to duck
and weave through his pursuers.

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:43.550
That means the whale still remains
trapped in Tokyo Bay.

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:48.060
Let's talk to our reporter on the scene.
Shiomi, how is the water?

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:52.940
Hi, this is Shiomi reporting
from Tokyo Bay!

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:59.360
The whale is just ahead.
Let's see if I can get close!

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:06.070
There it is, the famous Tokyo Bay whale!
Mr. Whale, one moment please!

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:10.370
A News 22 exclusive!
This is the Tokyo Bay whale!!

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:13.620
Please stay tuned for our exclusive
interview with Humpy!

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:16.170
We have a great show tonight.

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:17.960
We're going live
with the Tokyo Bay whale!

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:34.690
Hiromi, what's wrong?
You're out so early.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.860
Hmm... Yeah, well...

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:38.570
Worried about the whale?

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:42.530
I was just wondering if there
might be a better way to save it.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:44.400
We could be doing more harm than good.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:47.950
But it'll die if we don't
do anything, won't it?

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:49.870
Well, that's true, but...

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:58.920
Uh! I got it, Izumi!
We need a song!

00:12:59.090 --> 00:12:59.710
A song?

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:01.380
That's right, a song!

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:04.510
I have to tell Captain Goto!

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:06.680
Hiromi...

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:22.570
Mini Patrol

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:29.870
Prepare to cast off!

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.450
We appreciate your input, Captain.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.540
The Rescue Committee has
launched an undersea Labor.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:44.130
Every spectator here wonders:
What are their plans this time?

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.720
This is the SeaView.
I'm ready.

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:51.470
Good. You may begin.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:52.220
Roger.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:09.200
I hear it!
So this is the whale song.

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:10.030
Uh-huh.

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:12.370
- Uh! Look!
- Hm?

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:31.930
It's working!
The whale is leaving!

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:37.560
You did it, Hiromi.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:40.440
Humpback whales
communicate through sound.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:43.360
I knew it would react if it
heard other whales.

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:53.330
The End

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:56.240
Good morning!

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:56.870
Hey!

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:57.790
Good morning!

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:58.330
Morning.

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:00.710
Asuma, you're here early.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:01.960
Did you read it yet?

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.170
I see!

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:06.630
I don't understand why we
didn't get more coverage!

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:10.680
Did they mention anything about Hiromi?
He's the one who saved the day.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:12.680
Oh, no, not me.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:17.140
Of course you are! Turn on the TV.
I bet they're talking about him.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:18.020
Maybe.

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:22.900
Yeah! Here we go!

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:23.810
Hm?

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:25.400
Can you see it?

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:28.780
Yesterday the Rescue Committee led
the whale to freedom...

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:29.740
but it's come back.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:33.490
It was spotted early this morning,
and so our whale problem continues.

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:35.450
Duh!

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:38.330
The committee's headquarters
is mobbed by the media...

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:40.750
awaiting its response to
this late development.

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:43.170
Are you reopening the committee?

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:45.840
Will the whale keep returning?

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:48.300
Some people feel that
this is a waste of taxes.

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:51.300
Ms. Takao, say something!

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:54.510
Live morning debate!

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:57.640
Good morning.
Today's subject is the whale...

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:00.270
and we'll explore various solutions
to this troublesome problem.

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:01.850
Whale Problem in Tokyo Bay

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:03.400
The Whale Crisis

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:04.730
Opposition to the Rescue

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:07.730
The whale? Who cares anymore?
Leave him alone.

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:10.440
We already saved
that ungrateful creature once.

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:12.240
Why should we help him again?

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:16.410
I'm not paying a lot of taxes so they
can throw it away on some animal!

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:17.450
She's right!

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:25.420
128th session of the Diet

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:21.200
Mr. Prime Minister, how does your
administration intend to respond...

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:22.960
to the growing public criticism?

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:25.420
His Honorable Prime Minister.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:29.880
Er... well, for the time being,
we should just, uh...

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:35.590
The Diet has voted to eliminate the
Tokyo Bay Whale Rescue Committee.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:39.560
So, we're returning to our regular
rotation starting today.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:40.720
What!?

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:46.810
Now that you have some free time, I'd
like it if you could turn in those reports.

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:52.110
Uh! Hiromi!

00:16:58.030 --> 00:16:59.080
Hiromi...

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:04.160
Izumi, you think I'm being overly
sentimental about this whole thing?

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:06.290
Of course not!

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:19.140
I'm at Takeshiba Pier, on Tokyo Bay.

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:22.350
It's been eight days since the Rescue
Committee's humiliating failure.

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:26.440
The curious onlookers have left, ignoring
the mystery of the returning whale.

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:29.480
Has the whale had
its fifteen minutes of fame?

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:31.230
Is it doomed to fall
into oblivion?

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:36.650
But our dogged newshounds
have uncovered...

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:38.740
an intriguing piece
of information!

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:39.990
Look over there!

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:45.870
Wow! So the story was true!
There's a baby whale!

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:47.670
He's sooo tiny and cute!

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:49.790
C'mon, Noa, let me have a look!

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:51.380
No way!

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:54.760
Just for a second!
Oh, I can see it!

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:56.470
Can I have a look too?

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:57.510
Huh?

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:01.430
Ah, there it is!

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:06.180
Captain, ever since the baby whale
was spotted, I understand people...

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:07.770
have begun to call for another rescue.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:12.190
Oh, that. We're taking over the
rescue operation as of tomorrow.

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:16.150
What? Is that true, Captain?
Aren't you happy, Hiromi?

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:20.410
Wait a minute!
The ocean isn't in our jurisdiction!

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:26.660
Look, I don't need to tell you how
the public views our department, do I?

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:32.880
Let's see..."Losers' Club, hodgepodge,
outcasts, money pits, freeloaders."

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:36.670
No need to be so blunt.
But you're not far off.

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:38.130
So how in the world...?

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:42.850
Just listen. It's like this:
No one really expects us to succeed.

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:44.310
They think it's an impossible job.

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:47.680
So they figured
why not dump it on the losers...

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:48.480
and let them take the heat?

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:51.810
So we get to be their scapegoat
and make fools of ourselves?

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:53.770
That's about the size of it.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:55.940
There are limits to what
a man can take!

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:58.490
It's time we showed them
what we're made of!

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:00.570
Yes, let's show them.

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:08.450
My goodness! It's a wreck!

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:12.420
Please don't be so critical.
It started as scrap.

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:15.420
Shige and his crew worked
all night to salvage it!

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:17.960
I don't think that thing is gonna
stand up to the mission, is it?

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:22.300
As you can see,
the Rescue Committee lives again...

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:24.930
thanks to Special Vehicles,
Second Section, Division 2!

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:27.390
Good luck, Hiromi!
You can do it!

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:46.330
This is the speedboat.
We're ready.

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:51.750
All right, everyone.
Please stand by.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:03.800
I see them!
Dead ahead, 500 meters!

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:06.550
500 meters ahead, targets spotted.

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:09.640
Targets verified.
Here comes the sound.

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:22.320
This is the chopper.
No reaction from the whales.

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:24.780
Let me see if I can get a little closer.

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:28.620
Careful, Yamazaki. She's just given
birth, and may be overprotective.

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:30.040
I understand.

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:45.930
Uh!

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:55.270
What's wrong, Yamazaki?

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:56.940
Hiromi, are you okay?

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:02.110
I'm fine.

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:03.780
Are you still operational?

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:05.530
I am. Uh!

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:06.360
What's wrong?

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:10.490
It's the speakers. The collision
must have damaged the speakers.

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:15.750
I can't get any sound!

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:18.210
Well, that's that.
We better call it a day.

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:19.340
Return to the boat.

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.500
Hiromi, we'll try again tomorrow.

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:28.260
That sound... Hiromi, did you fix it?

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:31.760
That's not me.

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:32.470
Eh?

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:35.140
Helicopter here.
I see another whale in the open sea.

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:40.730
He's right!
There's another whale!

00:21:57.330 --> 00:21:58.500
It's an escort.

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:02.880
The humpbacks send a male to
guard the mother and newborn baby.

00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:05.420
He's the one that's singing.

00:22:15.850 --> 00:22:17.270
Look, they're...

00:22:26.940 --> 00:22:28.070
They're going home.

00:22:28.490 --> 00:22:32.160
So then what was all that
trouble for anyway?

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:45.590
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.710 --> 00:22:49.300
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.640 --> 00:22:55.560
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:05.070
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.190 --> 00:23:07.990
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:08.070 --> 00:23:12.570
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.240 --> 00:23:17.250
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:20.080
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:24.250
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:30.760
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:36.010
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:38.560
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.560 --> 00:23:41.770
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:45.860
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.230 --> 00:23:52.030
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:58.080
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.410 --> 00:24:04.710
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.210 --> 00:24:09.710
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.210 --> 00:24:09.710
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:13.720 --> 00:24:15.930
Noa's hometown in Hokkaido is
having a snow festival...

00:24:15.930 --> 00:24:18.060
and Division 2 is asked to lend a hand.

00:24:18.310 --> 00:24:22.600
I bet they need our Ingrams to
build some ice castles.

00:24:22.810 --> 00:24:24.650
Just leave it to me
and my delicate touch.

00:24:24.730 --> 00:24:26.650
And keep Ota away from
those ice blocks!

00:24:26.940 --> 00:24:30.110
But you think that's really
all they want from us?

00:24:30.280 --> 00:24:31.900
Hmm... it is a little suspicious.

00:24:32.450 --> 00:24:34.780
Next time:
"The Division Crosses the Sea."

00:24:34.950 --> 00:24:36.620
Target locked on!

00:24:35.450 --> 00:24:40.950
Next episode

00:24:35.450 --> 00:24:40.950
The Division Crosses the Sea
